mat="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO YOSHIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAKKO CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, SHIGEMITSU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO, YOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI SHIGEMITSU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO YOSHIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HAYASHI, SHIGEMITSU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO, YOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A drying method, a drying device, and a drying machine, capable of remarkably reducing a drying time by assigning the standby time for an article to be dried to a preliminary drying time in drying, wherein hot air is supplied to the drying machine so as to dry the article to be dried and, at the same time, hot air exhausted from the drying machine is led into a preliminary drying machine so as to preliminarily dry the article to be dried before drying, and then the article to be dried contained in the preliminary drying machine is fed to the drying machine for drying.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé de séchage, un dispositif de séchage et une machine de séchage capables de réduire de façon remarquable le temps de séchage par affectation du temps d'attente d'un article à sécher à un temps de séchage préliminaire pour le séchage, dans lequel de l'air chaud alimente la machine de séchage de manière à sécher l'article à sécher et, en même temps, de l'air chaud évacué de la machine de séchage est conduit jusque dans une machine de séchage préliminaire de manière à sécher de façon préliminaire l'article à sécher, avant séchage, et ensuite l'article à sécher contenu dans la machine de séchage préliminaire est acheminé jusqu'à la machine de séchage pour procéder au séchage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>